// The two values that are yours, in one place.
//
// They live in an xcconfig rather than in the project file so that changing them is a
// two-line edit in a text file instead of a hunt through Xcode's build settings, and so a
// `git diff` after you set them shows exactly one file.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Your bundle id. Must be globally unique across the App Store namespace, so use a
//    domain you control, reversed. This exact string has to match APNS_BUNDLE_ID in the
//    AgentSpine .env — APNs uses it as the topic, and a mismatch is rejected as
//    TopicDisallowed.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENTSPINE_BUNDLE_ID = com.houserphotography.AgentSpine

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID — the same one you put in APNS_TEAM_ID.
//    Find it at developer.apple.com/account under Membership details.
//
//    Leaving it empty also works: Xcode will ask you to pick a team the first time you
//    build, and write it into the project file. Setting it here keeps the project file
//    clean and makes the build reproducible from a fresh clone.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = 47A87M9KU5
